SUMMARY:Remember. Rebuild. Prepare. - Hurricane Preparedness Kit Day 2026
LOCATION:402 w laurel st Tampa \, FL 33607 United States
DESCRIPTION:Two years after the 2024 hurricanes\, many Florida families ar
 e still rebuilding\, while communities across Greater Tampa Bay continue p
 reparing for future storms. On Thursday\, September 24\, 2026\, Hurricane 
 Help Florida and StormResQ will host the inaugural Remember. Rebuild. Prep
 are. event at the Bob Buckhorn River Center. The event will bring resident
 s together with trusted disaster-recovery organizations\, local contractor
 s and community resources while raising awareness and support for families
  still living in damaged homes. The event is free and open to the public f
 rom 2:00 to 4:00 p.m. Hurricane Help Florida will distribute 500 resident 
 hurricane-preparedness kits and 250 pet-preparedness kits while supplies l
 ast. Guests may also make a 45 donation to attend from 12:00 to 2:00 p.m.\
 , which includes lunch from SaltBlock Hospitality and helps support contin
 ued rebuilding efforts. We are honored to welcome John Bennett\, Chief of 
 Staff for the City of Tampa\, along with nonprofit partners\, volunteers\,
  community leaders and local businesses committed to strengthening Greater
  Tampa Bays disaster preparedness and long-term recovery. You can register
  to attend at: Remember. Rebuild. Prepare \n\nPermalink: https://www.tampa
 .gov/node/193986
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/193986
END:VEVENT
