SUMMARY:Next Level Workshop - Sew Seen: Stitching New Narratives with Nnek
 a Jones
LOCATION:120 W Gasparilla Plaza Tampa \, FL 33602 United States
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, Oct 3 - Sunday\, Oct 4  10:00 AM  4:00 PM (2 classe
 s) Ages 18  Beginner-Intermediate Level Sew Seen: Stitching New Narratives
  invites participants to explore storytelling through contemporary mixed m
 edia techniques that combine printmaking\, painting\, and embroidery. Insp
 ired by Nneka Jones work featured in Avant Garde: Remarkable Women in the 
 Permanent Collection at the Tampa Museum of Art\, students will experiment
  with layering imagery\, texture\, and thread to transform everyday visual
 s into expressive works of art. Throughout the workshop\, participants wil
 l learn foundational stitching and image-transfer techniques while develop
 ing their own visual narratives in a collaborative and supportive environm
 ent. The course encourages creative exploration\, self-expression\, and a 
 fresh perspective on fiber art within contemporary art practices. All supp
 lies are provided\, including a custom supply kit curated by the artist\, 
 a value of 100. \n\nPermalink: https://www.tampa.gov/node/193671
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/193671
END:VEVENT
